WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.478
- Hello, everyone.

00:00:08.478 --> 00:00:09.360
I hope that you're doing well,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.930
and thanks for joining us.

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:14.797
It's my great pleasure to
introduce Dr. Cindy Nguyen,

00:00:14.797 --> 00:00:17.941
who is a wonderful colleague,
friend and a human being.

00:00:17.941 --> 00:00:21.640
Dr. Nguyen earned her PhD
in History at UC Berkeley

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.660
and specializes in the history of Vietnam,

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.383
Southeast Asian print
culture and libraries.

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:30.020
Currently she's a postdoctoral fellow

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:33.590
in international humanities
in the department of history

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:37.100
and the Cogut Institute for
Humanities at Brown University

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.890
where she teaches innovative
virtual reality based courses

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.633
on Southeast Asian history.

00:00:43.779 --> 00:00:45.741
And her book manuscript,

00:00:45.741 --> 00:00:48.801
"Reading and Misreading:
The Social Life of Libraries

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:53.801
"and Colonial Control
in Vietnam, 1865-1958"

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.040
examines the cultural
and political history

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.970
of libraries in Hanoi and Saigon

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.470
from the French colonial period

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.600
through to the decolonization of libraries

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.070
through the lens of cultural imperialism,

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.870
national legitimacy, and social
practices of public reading.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:15.110
She has presented for
scholarship internationally,

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:18.850
including in the US,
Vietnam, and Singapore.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:19.927
In her essay,

00:01:19.927 --> 00:01:23.107
"The Social Life of the
Hanoi Central Library:

00:01:23.107 --> 00:01:26.653
"Reading Cultures in
Public Space, 1919 to 1941"

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.263
won the Association for Asian Studies'

00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:34.950
Pattana Kitiarsa Southeast
Asian Council Prize in 2020.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.420
In addition to being a scholar, Dr. Nguyen

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:41.930
is also a digital humanist,
an artist, a poet,

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.900
a translator, a filmmaker,

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:47.490
a publisher, a feminist and a refugee.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.790
She seamlessly weaves these dimensions

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:54.060
into provocative and
beautiful multimedia work,

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.770
including short films that meditate

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:59.050
on intergenerational transmissions

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:01.560
of language, love and loss.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:05.140
Dr. Nguyen is currently working
on a poetic documentary film

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.430
on the language of Vietnamese
refugee remembrance

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:09.740
and history.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:12.610
And since this brief
introduction does not do justice

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.210
to the breadth and depth of
Dr. Nguyen's intellectual

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:18.630
and creative endeavors,
please do visit her websites,

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.250
and I'll drop those in the chat for you

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:24.580
for more information and
access to her wonderful work.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.965
Today, Dr. Nguyen's talk is titled,

00:02:27.965 --> 00:02:29.047
"The Politics of Good Reading:

00:02:29.047 --> 00:02:32.517
"Libraries and the Public
in Late Colonial Vietnam."

00:02:33.566 --> 00:02:35.730
Please join me in welcoming Dr. Nguyen.

